-- statement:
--   Let $N\ne0$, fix a real function $\nu$ on $\mathbb Z/N\mathbb Z$, independent masks and AP weight families for two Boolean copies, and a distinguished face $j$. Assume each copy satisfies the untouched-face bounds against its own masked majorant. For every finite-type presentation of the terminal stage parameter, the fully iterated form of the heterogeneous two-copy system is the mean of the centered product on $j$ times the linear-forms product selected by the copy-dependent terminal exponent.
